      "hints": [
        "Recognise $9^x=3^{2x}$ and substitute $u=3^x$.",
        "Solve the quadratic $u^2=u+12$, rejecting any value impossible for $u=3^x>0$.",
        "Use logarithms to solve the remaining equation $3^x=u$ and round only the final value to 2 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Rewrite $9^x$ as a power with base $3$ using the rule $(a^m)^n = (a^n)^m$:\n$$9^x = (3^2)^x = (3^x)^2$$",
        "Substitute into the given equation $9^x = 3^x + 12$:\n$$(3^x)^2 = 3^x + 12$$",
        "Let $u = 3^x$ (where $u > 0$ for all real $x$):\n$$u^2 - u - 12 = 0$$",
        "Factor the quadratic equation:\n$$(u - 4)(u + 3) = 0$$",
        "Solve for $u$:\n$$u = 4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad u = -3$$",
        "Substitute back $u = 3^x$ and analyze each case:\n- For $u = -3$:\n$$3^x = -3$$\nSince $3^x > 0$ for all real values of $x$, this equation has no real solutions.\n- For $u = 4$:\n$$3^x = 4$$",
        "Take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n$$\\ln(3^x) = \\ln 4$$\n$$x\\ln 3 = \\ln 4$$\n$$x = \\dfrac{\\ln 4}{\\ln 3}$$",
        "Compute the numerical value:\n$$x = \\dfrac{\\ln 4}{\\ln 3} \\approx \\dfrac{1.386294}{1.098612} \\approx 1.261860$$",
        "Round to 2 decimal places:\n$$x \\approx 1.26$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Solving Exponential and Logarithmic Equations": "With $u=3^x$, $9^x=3^x+12$ becomes $u^2-u-12=0$; the positive root $u=4$ gives $x=\\log_3 4=1.26$."
        },
